      'The capture opens the older Rules workspace and selects a demo rule.',
      'The overview displays a sample condition and says no action was recorded.',
      'It does not demonstrate applying the rule or current TUI navigation.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: '10-one-mailbox-three-interfaces',
    title: 'See separate TUI, CLI, and agent recordings',
    duration: '35s',
    description: 'An edited montage cuts between a TUI mailbox, a CLI search, and a recorded agent session.',
    provenance: 'Composite of separate TUI, CLI, and agent captures using synthetic mail. The edits do not show a continuous handoff or prove shared-state synchronization; the web client is not shown.',
    steps: [
      'The first segment shows the TUI mailbox and a selected message.',
      'A separate segment shows a shell search and its results.',
      'The final segment shows an agent prompt and search. Treat these as distinct recordings, not one continuous session.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: '11-mxr-is-written-in-rust',
    title: 'A montage of mxr client screens',
    duration: '32s',
    description: 'This composite cuts between TUI, CLI, and agent screens; it does not show source code or a live client handoff.',
    provenance: 'Composite of separate synthetic-mail TUI, CLI, and agent recordings. The web client is not shown, and the recording does not demonstrate the Rust implementation.',
    steps: [
      'The montage shows a TUI mailbox and message view.',
      'It cuts to a separate CLI search and a recorded agent search.',
      'The sequence is illustrative editing, not a continuous session or implementation walkthrough.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: '12-agent-previews-a-change',
    title: 'Preview an archive selection in the CLI',
    duration: '12s',
    description: 'The CLI dry-runs an archive search and lists the two selected threads and two messages before any change.',
    provenance: 'Recorded CLI capture against synthetic mail. Despite the old asset name, no agent appears in this clip.',
    steps: [
      'The command selects unread messages from a synthetic notes-list address.',
      'The --dry-run output says it would archive two threads containing two messages.',
      'The preview does not apply the archive action.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: '13-two-accounts-one-mailbox',
    title: 'List two synthetic accounts, then search one address',
    duration: '14s',
    description: 'The CLI lists two synthetic accounts and then searches messages from one demo address.',
    provenance: 'Recorded CLI capture using two synthetic accounts with fake sync and send settings.',
    steps: [
      'The accounts command lists Demo Personal and Demo Work.',
      'A separate search uses the notes address and displays matching rows.',
      'The search does not specify an account, so this clip does not establish combined cross-account scope or real-provider behavior.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: '15-searches-attachments',
    title: 'Find messages with attachments',
    duration: '12s',
    description: 'A CLI search filters synthetic mail for one sender and messages with attachments, returning two rows.',
    provenance: 'Recorded CLI capture against synthetic mail. It demonstrates search results only, not downloading or filing an attachment.',
    steps: [
      'The query combines a sender filter with has:attachment.',
      'The terminal lists two matching messages with subjects and dates.',
      'No attachment is downloaded, opened, or added to a manifest in this recording.',
    ],
  },
];
---

<div class="video-gallery">
  {clips.map((clip) => (
    <article>
      <video
        controls
        playsinline
        preload="none"
        poster={`/videos/${clip.id}.jpg`}
        aria-label={`${clip.title} recording`}
      >
        <source src={`/videos/${clip.id}.mp4`} type="video/mp4" />
        <p>Your browser cannot play this video. <a href={`/videos/${clip.id}.mp4`}>Open the recording</a>.</p>
      </video>
      <div class="video-gallery-heading">
        <h2>{clip.title}</h2>
        <span>{clip.duration}</span>
      </div>
      <p>{clip.description}</p>
      <p class="video-gallery-provenance">{clip.provenance}</p>
      <details>
        <summary>Read the recording notes</summary>
        <ol>
          {clip.steps.map((step) => <li>{step}</li>)}
        </ol>
      </details>
      <a href={`/videos/${clip.id}.mp4`}>Open video: {clip.title}</a>
    </article>
  ))}
</div>
